Z||000000||beer_stud_21||02-09-2001||08:09 PM||||Hey all.  I've had my car for 1 week so far and am just staring to get to work on it.  I've got some pretty basic questions for you all.  <P>1) How is the best way to get the little rivit things out of the drivers side rear wheel well?  I'm trying to get to the air restrictor box so i can tear it out.  I got this car for $300.00 and it needs LOTS of work.  The air filter box was totally rusted to hell so i yanked it out. <P>2) Is there a trick to removing the trim pieces?<P>3) How much should an Ignition control module cost me?  I was told somewhere around 22 bucks, but today I called around locally including to GM and got price quotes ranging from $66-$101.  The fiero store has them for $35.00 which is better but I didnt think I was going to have to pay double for a part at Napa.  I would hate to see what an ICM for an MR2 would cost....  lol<P>Thats it for now...  Thanks all..<P>-Marlin||||reg||1
Z||000001||MrPBody||02-09-2001||08:54 PM||||Wheel-well rivets are a pain.  Some of them have phillips-head pins which seldom unscrew.  Others have a push-in pin which I can usually pull out with diagonal cutting pliers or end-nippers.  If all else fails, I bite them off with nippers and replace them with Motormite rivets.<P>Molding: see <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/008384.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/008384.html</A> <BR>||||reg||1
